WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.628
An expired certificate is almost always an

2
00:00:02.628 --> 00:00:05.350
ownership problem before
it's a technical one.

3
00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:08.525
So every certificate gets
a home and a named owner.

4
00:00:08.525 --> 00:00:12.916
The platform's policy folders mirror
the workbook's certificate classes,

5
00:00:12.916 --> 00:00:16.012
so where a certificate lives
tells you how it renews.

6
00:00:16.012 --> 00:00:19.666
Owners come from Entra groups,
and, if the agency uses it,

7
00:00:19.666 --> 00:00:25.350
the ServiceNow app can tie certificates to
the same configuration items as the CMDB.

8
00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:29.415
And one alert matters most: a
certificate nearing expiry with no

9
00:00:29.415 --> 00:00:33.310
renewal path is an incident while
there's still time to fix it.
